      "outputs": [],
      "title": "Note: Getting Started with RefPacks",
      "properties": {},
      "widgets_values": [
        "First, choose your models, clip, and vae first. Any H3 model should work, but starting with the default ComfyUI H3 Ref2VA models can be a good start. You can use LoRAs or bypass the node if you want the stock model.\n\nSecond, create one or more RefPacks. Check the 02_Prepare_Character_Or_Outfit.json workflow for an example. \n\nThird, choose and chain the RefPacks you want to use. Make sure to select the type, such as Character, Outfit, Location, and Motion, depending on what your RefPack does. \n\nFinally, choose a length in frames or use the duration helper node (BExplains H3 Duration). This workflow can produce both images and workflow for H3. Choosing a length below 5 frames will generate images and a length above that produces a video if your generation type is Auto. You can override this behavior in the encoder node. \n\n"
      ],
      "widgets_values_named": {
        "text": "First, choose your models, clip, and vae first. Any H3 model should work, but starting with the default ComfyUI H3 Ref2VA models can be a good start. You can use LoRAs or bypass the node if you want the stock model.\n\nSecond, create one or more RefPacks. Check the 02_Prepare_Character_Or_Outfit.json workflow for an example. \n\nThird, choose and chain the RefPacks you want to use. Make sure to select the type, such as Character, Outfit, Location, and Motion, depending on what your RefPack does. \n\nFinally, choose a length in frames or use the duration helper node (BExplains H3 Duration). This workflow can produce both images and workflow for H3. Choosing a length below 5 frames will generate images and a length above that produces a video if your generation type is Auto. You can override this behavior in the encoder node. \n\n"
      },
      "color": "#222",
      "bgcolor": "#000"
    },
